  ------------------------------------------------------------
    the programme
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      0:00  I   THE LAMP      the blencong is lit: bronze bowl,
                              living flame. gong ageng, one
                              suling breath
      0:06      (rise)        pull back through the cloth; the
                              gunungan tree-of-life is planted
                              at centre screen
      0:16  II  THE COURT     the refined hero enters and bows.
                              saron balungan, kenong & kempul,
                              light interlocking kotekan
      0:40  III THE DEMON     a raksasa swells out of the dark,
                              lifted toward the lamp, shadow
                              blurring large. low ostinato,
                              driving kendang
      1:04  IV  THE BATTLE    demon lunges, club swings, the
                              hero's arrow flies. full ensemble
      1:16      (through)     the dalang's side: gold-leaf
                              puppets glowing in lamplight; the
                              gong ageng struck on the beat;
                              the arrow strikes home
      1:32  V   THE FALL      the demon topples into the banana
                              log; the hero bows; the gunungan
                              returns. a single gender, gong tail
      1:52  VI  DAWN          morning light floods the cloth,
                              shadows dissolve to umber, the
                              lamp dies. one last gong, silence

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how to run
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Double-click intro.html in Edge or Chrome on Windows 10
      or 11, wait for "CLICK" (a few seconds while the shaders
      compile and the 48 kHz soundtrack renders), then click
      to go fullscreen. No server, no browser flags, no
      network. ESC exits fullscreen. A discrete GPU is
      expected. Tested on Edge (ANGLE/D3D11) with an RTX 5090
      (~0.8 ms/frame at 1080p for the shadow screen).

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    inside
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      The audience side of the screen is a 2D composite whose
      rendering trick is real shadow physics: every puppet has
      a distance d from the cloth, its shadow is magnified by
      L/(L-d) and its penumbra grows with d. Pressed to the
      screen it casts a crisp 1:1 shadow; lifted toward the
      lamp it swells and softens. That one rule drives the
      demon's threat, the battle blur and the focus pulls.
      Perforations (tatahan) and the gunungan's carved tree,
      split gate (candi bentar) and wing flares let the lamp
      light back through as bright shapes in the dark leather.

      The puppets are flat SDF figures in the wayang profile:
      long nose, downcast eye, tall crown or wild hair and
      fangs, two-segment arms on rods, a bell skirt; control
      rods (tuding) run down to the banana log (debog). The
      dalang's side reuses the same fields as painted backlit
      gold-leaf leather with glowing lacework and batik skirts.
      The gong ageng is a shaded bronze disc with a raised boss
      (pencu), turned rings and a specular glint on a carved
      red-and-gold rancakan frame, struck by a ball mallet.

      The soundtrack is a procedural gamelan in a pelog-like
      scale, rendered one pixel per stereo sample at 48 kHz
      into a float FBO and read back through the shared 4-line
      Householder FDN reverb and compressor. Struck-bronze
      voices sum inharmonic partials plus a detuned pair for
      the ombak beat; a colotomic gong/kenong/kempul cycle
      gives the form, the balungan feeds the kotekan, and the
      kendang drives the battle. Picture and score share one
      bar clock. Post adds DOF, mip bloom, a filmic curve,
      grain, typography and a warm dawn grade.

